        "date": "2026-11-12T08:42:58Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(thread): external threads on a boss at the operation level\n\nThe Thread operation gains `external`: its list then holds bosses\n(major radius, top, shoulder), read from the model by Detect holes\n(`drilling::recognize_bosses`: the hole recogniser's law with the facing\nvote inverted, stepped walls never folded) and passed to the kernel's\nexternal ride pinned by #1005.\n\nA tool beside a boss is judged without the part's silhouette:\n- crest law: the tangency verdict against each boss's MINOR circle\n  (ISO 965-1 design root, 0.6134 x pitch) - the drawn wall is not the\n  wall the crests answer to (#1071's lesson read for a boss);\n- root law: the solid law with the cutter narrowed by the external\n  depth - roots, tip, shank and holder against the whole part;\n- neighbour law (new): the crest ring at full radius against every\n  facet that is not the threaded boss's own wall, no thread allowance.\n\nThe air law (#992's external analogue): every position the feeds take\nthe tool through is read in the stock the program ahead leaves; stock\nstanding under the tool's disc outside the boss refuses the thread by\nname. Unknown is refused.\n\nThe door refuses a boss no thicker than the thread is deep and a thread\nlonger than the mill reaches beside a boss. The program simulation\nsweeps an external thread at its external root radius. The Thread page\ngets the external checkbox, Detect bosses and a per-row Remove; the MCP\ntools carry the flag through the existing params and detect_holes.\n\nGoldens: thread_mill_external_m8_multi_form.cl/.nc,\nthread_mill_external_m10_single_form.cl.\n\nFixes #985\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
