      "message": "Merge refreshed #1045 (issue/992-thread-undrilled @ 6dd3f773) into issue/985-external-threads\n\nConflicts: operation/generate.rs, operation/thread_op.rs, operation/mod.rs,\nstock_sim.rs, tests/mcp.rs. Resolutions:\n- generate.rs Thread arm: internal threads take the parent's #1071 reading\n  (thread_rims::major_rims behind walls_round); external threads keep #985's\n  thread_boss::crest_region on the minor circle. Both entry laws kept. The\n  neighbour law and the parent's tap_core acquit are both kept.\n- thread_op.rs: the parent's `bores` grant is the internal solid law; it\n  returns no grant for an external thread (a boss is no bore). #985's\n  `root_cutter` returns for external threads only (narrowed by the external\n  depth), so the grant and a narrowed cutter are never stacked\n  (docs/decisions/894-thread-mill.md, \"The refresh against main\", item 2).\n- mod.rs: keep both module lists. stock_sim.rs: the parent's electrode arm\n  kept; the cutter arm reads thread_op::sim_radius (#985).\n- mcp.rs: both tests kept. coarse_rims.rs, thread_mill_rim.rs: `external:\n  false` on the parent's new Thread literals.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
