      },
      "message": "feat(thread): refuse an external thread on a boss that is not round\n\nThe crest law reads each boss's minor circle and the neighbour law passes\nthe boss's own wall, both taking that wall for a circle. A hex stud or a\nsquare post stands its flats inside the drawn circle, where the teeth\nwould cut them with no law reading them. thread_boss::not_round applies\nthe internal side's walls_round test (verify::hole_is_round, the solid\nlaw's sagitta test) to the boss wall, and generate refuses a boss that\nfails it by name. Pinned by\nthread_boss::a_hex_stud_is_no_round_boss_and_is_refused_by_name; the\ndecision is in docs/decisions/985-external-threads.md.\n\nRefs #985\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
